### FORBIDDEN WORDS & PHRASES

**Clichés to Avoid**
- "Leverage"
- "Synergy"
- "Best in class"
- "Cutting edge"
- "Revolutionary"
- "Game changing"
- "Seamless"
- "Robust"
- "Empower" (use sparingly if at all)
- "Journey" (overused—use alternatives like "path," "experience")

**Mental Health Specific Avoidances**
- "Crazy," "insane," "nuts" (ableist)
- "Commit suicide" (use "died by suicide")
- "Successful suicide" (use "died by suicide")
- "Failed attempt" (use "suicide attempt")
- "Normal" vs "abnormal" (use "typical" or "common")

**Healthcare Claims to Avoid**
- Guarantees of outcomes ("We will cure...")
- Comparative claims without substantiation
- Superlatives without evidence ("best," "fastest," "most effective")

**Formatting Forbidden**
- Hyphens in copy (rewrite to avoid)
- ALL CAPS for emphasis
- Multiple exclamation points!!!
- Excessive bold/italic

